  "id": "eitheror-thinking",
  "term": "either–or thinking",
  "definition": "Either–or thinking is a way of viewing a situation as if there are only two opposing options, so that one benefit seems possible only at the cost of the other. In this packet, it refers to treating enjoyment and skill learning in physical education as mutually exclusive instead of potentially working together.",
